<title>SWITZERLAND: CSFB raises Novartis earnings estimates.</title>
<headline>CSFB raises Novartis earnings estimates.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston said it had raised its earnings estimates for Novartis AG to reflect the weak Swiss franc, strong pharmaceutical sales, good progress in achieving merger synergy and a solid research presentation.</p>
<p>It gave these updated forecasts (previous in brackets):</p>
<p>		     1997     1998	1999	2000	 2001</p>
<p> EPS	     77 (72)   89 (82)  100 (93)  107 (102)  113 (108)</p>
<p> EBITDA	 123 (115) 138 (128) 152 (142) 160 (153)  166 (160)</p>
<p>Sales</p>
<p> (Sfr million)  31,815   34,220    36,441     38,361     40,148</p>
<p>Oper profit</p>
<p> after synergies 6,936    7,952     8,824	9,289	9,628</p>
<p> Net profit	5,304    6,128     6,864	7,354	7,782</p>
<p> Dividend (Sfr)     25	 29	 33	    35	   37</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
